tags: demo structure
My first structured page
title end

paragraph start
This page shows how a file is built from nested sections. Every line sits inside a named block, and the checker refuses loose text.
paragraph end

section start
title start
Why blocks
title end
paragraph start
A block has a start line, a body and an end line with the same name. Because blocks can hold other blocks, a chapter is simply a section that holds its own title, its text and its sub-sections.
paragraph end

section start
title start
Sub-sections nest
title end
paragraph start
style: bold
color: green
Styling is declared on the lines right under the start line. It is only a hint, and a terminal shows bold, italic, underline and color.
paragraph end
section end

section start
title start
Numbers are computed
title end
paragraph start
Nobody types 1.2 or 2.1. The viewer counts the sections by nesting depth, so moving a section never leaves a wrong number behind.
paragraph end
section end

section end

